    "body": "Let $\\mathbb{P}_2$ denote the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most 2 in the variable $t$, and let $\\mathbb{M}_{ 2 \\times2}$ denote the vector space of all $2 \\times2$ matrices. Consider a linear transformation:\n\n\\[T: \\mathbb{P}_2 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{M}_{ 2 \\times2} \\quad \\textrm{given by} \\quad T(p(t)) = \\left[\\begin{array}{ll}\np(0) & p'(0) \\\\\np(1) & p'(1)\n\\end{array}\\right].\\]\n\n(1) Find $T(at^2+bt+c)$.\n\n(2) Find a polynomial $p(t)$ in $\\mathbb{P}_2$ such that $T(p(t)) = \\left[\\begin{array}{ll}\n1 & 2 \\\\\n4 & 4\n\\end{array}\\right].$\n\n(3) Find a basis for the range of $T$. ",
